---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { links } from "../data/site";

const updated = "29 October 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What Pesa Clarity keeps on your phone, what its server holds, and your rights."
>
  <article class="container privacy-page">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated {updated}.</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        Pesa Clarity works out your budget on your phone. Your transactions,
        messages and statements never leave it. Our server does three narrow
        jobs and never sees a transaction.
      </p>

      <h2>What stays on your phone</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Messages from the banks and wallets you choose. Messages from every
          other sender are ignored and never stored.
        </li>
        <li>
          On iPhone, messages come from a Shortcuts automation you set up. Each
          one waits in a file only Pesa Clarity can open until the app reads it,
          for at most 35 days.
        </li>
        <li>
          The fields read from those messages: amount, date, payee, balance and
          fee. The raw message text is discarded after reading.
        </li>
        <li>
          Statement PDFs. Their passwords are used once, in memory, then
          discarded. PDFs are never uploaded.
        </li>
        <li>Budgets, debts, goals, payees, categories and every insight.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        All of this sits in an encrypted database. The key is held by your
        phone's secure hardware and released only after you unlock the app with
        your PIN, fingerprint or Face ID.
      </p>

      <h2>What our server holds</h2>
      <dl>
        <dt>Sign-in</dt>
        <dd>
          Your account id, the email or Google account you sign in with, and
          when you signed up, in and out. You can also use the app without an
          account.
        </dd>
        <dt>Encrypted backups</dt>
        <dd>
          If you choose our vault, backups are encrypted on your phone with your
          passphrase before upload. We hold only the encrypted file and cannot
          read it. The server checks with Google (Android) or Apple (iPhone)
          that each backup comes from the genuine app; neither sees the backup.
          You can back up to your own Google Drive, your phone, an SD card or
          Files on iPhone instead.
        </dd>
        <dt>Model updates</dt>
        <dd>
          If "improve the app" is on, your phone sends clipped, noised updates
          to the categoriser, combined with other users' before we can see them.
          Never your transactions. You can switch this off at any time.
        </dd>
      </dl>

      <h2>Exchange rates</h2>
      <p>
        To count money in other currencies, the app downloads today's exchange
        rates from a public rates service. The request carries only your base
        currency's code, such as KES; the service sees your IP address, as any
        website does. You can set your own rates instead.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>The app asks on first run, and you can change these any time:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Improve the app (federated updates): on by default.</li>
        <li>Contribute to licensed models: off unless you opt in.</li>
        <li>Anonymous crash reports: off unless you opt in.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Pesa Clarity has no ads, no analytics and no third-party trackers.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the Kenya Data Protection Act 2019 you can ask to see, correct or
        delete the data we hold about you, and object to automated decisions. We
        will answer within 30 days. You can delete your account from inside the
        app.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no cookies, runs no analytics and loads nothing from
        other servers. Fonts are served from this site. The web host may keep
        standard request logs, such as IP address and time, for security.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        {/* TODO: add the data protection contact once the controller is registered with the ODPC. */}
        Ask in public on <a href={links.github}>GitHub</a>, or report a security
        issue privately using the security policy there.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy-page {
    padding-block: var(--space-7) var(--space-8);
  }

  h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }

  dt {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
